# Environment variables for claude-code-ghcp-sdk.
#
# How to use this file:
# - Nothing loads it automatically. Export a variable in your shell, or put it
#   in front of one command:  TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=600000 ./bin/claude-ghcp
# - Every line is commented out, so sourcing the file as it is changes nothing.
# - Each entry gives its default, or says it is required. Its commented
#   NAME=value line shows either that default or an example to replace.
# - Command-line options win over these variables.
# - Each number in sections 2 and 3 must be a positive integer. Any other
#   value stops the bridge at startup.
#
# Sections:
#   1. Direct launcher (bin/claude-ghcp)
#   2. Bridge tuning (every bridge; changing one replaces the persistent bridge)
#   3. Only for a bridge you start by hand (npm run bridge)
#   4. LiteLLM client (bin/claude-litellm)
#   5. LiteLLM gateway (scripts/start-litellm.sh)
#
# Left out on purpose:
# - BRIDGE_INSTANCE_ID and BRIDGE_LEASE_DIR: the persistent bridge sets them
#   for itself.
# - BRIDGE_TEST_FAULTS: a fault injector for tests.
# - COPILOT_SDK_DEFAULT_CONNECTION: the Copilot SDK's transport selector; leave
#   it unset.
# - VERIFY_HOOK_LOG: used only inside the verification harness.
# - Claude Code's own ANTHROPIC_* variables: the launchers write them into the
#   settings file they pass to Claude Code. `npm run current-provider` only
#   reads them.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Direct launcher (bin/claude-ghcp)
#
# Read by the launcher each time it starts. None of these replaces a running
# persistent bridge, except GHCP_BRIDGE_PORT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copilot model Claude Code starts on. --ghcp-model overrides it.
# List the model IDs your account can use with ./bin/ghcp-models.
# The launcher exits if the model is not in your Copilot catalog.
# Default: claude-sonnet-5.
# Change when: you want another default model without passing --ghcp-model.
# GHCP_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Fixed loopback port for the launcher's bridge, both the persistent one and
# the private -p one. Same as --bridge-port. It must be from 1 to 65535.
# Default: none. The launcher picks a free port.
# Change when: something else must reach the bridge at a known address, such
# as LiteLLM's api_base. Changing it replaces the persistent bridge, and every
# shell that should share that bridge needs the same value.
# GHCP_BRIDGE_PORT=4142

# 1 turns on Claude Code's native MCP tool search (ToolSearch). 0 keeps it off.
# Either way the bridge sends every MCP tool's full schema to Copilot with
# every request. Any value other than 0 or 1 stops the launch.
# See docs/COMPATIBILITY.md#feature-lookup.
# Default: 0.
# Change when: you want to try ToolSearch with a large set of MCP tools.
# GHCP_NATIVE_TOOL_SEARCH=0

# Real Claude Code executable the launchers run (a path or a command name).
# Default: the first `claude` on PATH that is not one of this repository's
# launchers. ./bin/ghcp-doctor reads it too.
# Change when: Claude Code is not on PATH, or you have several installs. It
# must not point at claude, claude-ghcp, claude-litellm or claude-current from
# any checkout of this repository.
# CLAUDE_CODE_BIN=/absolute/path/to/claude

# Claude Code's fullscreen renderer. Passing settings on the command line would
# otherwise switch it off, so both launchers (claude-ghcp and claude-litellm)
# export CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1 when it is unset. A value you set yourself,
# even an empty one, is kept.
# Default: 1 (set by the launchers).
# Change when: you want the classic renderer. Set it to 0 or to an empty value.
# CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1

# Directory of the persistent bridge used by every launch except -p: its
# registry (bridge.json), lock, bridge.log, per-launch settings, leases and
# records of replaced bridges. The bridge also runs in this directory.
# Default: ~/Library/Caches/claude-code-ghcp-sdk on macOS,
#          ${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-~/.cache}/claude-code-ghcp-sdk elsewhere.
# Use an absolute path: ~ is not expanded here.
# Change when: you need a separate set of bridges, for example for tests or a
# second profile. A different directory gets its own bridge; it does not
# replace the other one.
# GHCP_DAEMON_DIR=/absolute/path/to/claude-code-ghcp-sdk

# Standard variables the launchers also read:
# - XDG_CACHE_HOME (default ~/.cache): base of the default GHCP_DAEMON_DIR
#   outside macOS.
# - TMPDIR (default /tmp): where each launch makes its temporary directory.
#   For claude-ghcp -p it holds the private bridge's log and the settings file.
#   For claude-litellm it holds the settings file.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Bridge tuning
#
# Read by every bridge: the persistent one, the private -p one, and one you
# start by hand.
#
# Changing one of these replaces the persistent bridge at the next launch
# other than -p. The persistent bridge keeps a fingerprint of the values it
# started with (its configuration fingerprint), and a launch whose values
# differ starts a new bridge. This happens even when the new value equals the
# default, because an exported variable counts differently from an unset one.
# The replaced bridge keeps serving the sessions already open on it, with the
# old values. It exits once no launcher that started on it is still running
# and it has had no request for RETIRED_IDLE_MS. See
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#persistent-bridge-and-retirement.
#
# The fingerprint also counts every other variable whose name starts with
# COPILOT_ or MAX_, and GH_TOKEN, GITHUB_TOKEN, GH_CONFIG_DIR, HTTP_PROXY,
# HTTPS_PROXY, NO_PROXY and HOME (upper-case names only). The Copilot runtime
# inherits these.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Largest request body the bridge accepts, in bytes. A larger body gets
# 400 invalid_request_error.
# Default: 268435456 (256 MiB).
# Change when: you want to cap memory use, or very large image and PDF
# histories are rejected.
# MAX_BODY_BYTES=268435456

# When the bridge has to rebuild a conversation it has no Copilot session for
# (for example after a bridge restart, or a resumed or forked session it has
# not seen), it replays at most this many bytes of the saved history, keeping
# the newest messages. Older ones are dropped and logged as
# bridge.history_replay_truncated. This does not change the model's context
# window.
# Default: 268435456 (256 MiB).
# Change when: you want a resumed or forked session to replay less.
# MAX_REPLAY_BYTES=268435456

# Most tool results one request may send back at once. A request with more
# fails with 500 api_error.
# Default: 32.
# Change when: a model legitimately makes more than 32 tool calls at once.
# MAX_TOOL_RESULTS=32

# Most Copilot sessions (conversations and subagents) the bridge keeps open.
# Beyond that it closes the least recently used idle one; the next message
# to it reopens it.
# Default: 64.
# Change when: many parallel sessions or subagents keep closing each other.
# MAX_STATES=64

# A Copilot session with no turn running and no tool call pending is closed
# once it has gone this long unused. The bridge checks this whenever a request
# arrives. The next message to that conversation reopens it.
# Default: 1800000 (30 minutes).
# Change when: you want long pauses to stay warm (raise) or to free memory
# sooner (lower).
# STATE_IDLE_TTL_MS=1800000

# How long a tool result waits for Copilot to register the matching tool call.
# Default: 10000 (10 seconds).
# Change when: bridge.unregistered_tool_call appears for tools that were
# declared.
# PENDING_TOOL_WAIT_MS=10000

# Time limit for creating or resuming a Copilot session, or for changing its
# reasoning effort. When it runs out, the request fails with 500 api_error and
# bridge.session_operation_failed is logged. Separate from the turn limits.
# Default: 60000 (60 seconds).
# Change when: a slow Copilot runtime keeps hitting it.
# SESSION_OPERATION_TIMEOUT_MS=60000

# A turn fails after this long without progress from the main model (text,
# reasoning or tool-call input). New output resets the timer.
# Default: 300000 (5 minutes). Maximum 2147483647.
# Change when: a model reasons silently for longer than 5 minutes.
# TURN_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=300000

# Hard limit on one turn, even while it is still streaming. It never resets.
# Default: 1800000 (30 minutes). Maximum 2147483647.
# Change when: single turns legitimately run longer than 30 minutes.
# TURN_MAX_DURATION_MS=1800000
#
# If either turn limit fires while Copilot is waiting to retry an upstream 429
# or 5xx, the turn fails as 429 or 529, which Claude Code retries. Otherwise it
# fails as 500 api_error. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#upstream-errors.

# Best-effort wait for each step of closing a Copilot session (abort,
# disconnect, delete).
# Default: 5000 (5 seconds).
# Change when: cleanup on a slow runtime keeps being cut off.
# CLEANUP_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# A replaced (retired) bridge exits after this long with no request, once no
# launcher that started on it is still running.
# Default: 3600000 (1 hour). Maximum 2147483647.
# Change when: you want old bridges gone sooner (lower), or /background jobs
# pause for longer than an hour (raise).
# RETIRED_IDLE_MS=3600000

# Log level of the Copilot runtime: none, error, warning, info, debug or all.
# It does not affect the bridge's own diagnostic lines, which are always
# written and carry no prompt or response text. The runtime's own output also
# lands in the bridge's log. This repository does not check whether higher
# levels write prompt content there.
# Default: error.
# Change when: you are debugging the Copilot runtime. Set it back afterwards.
# LOG_LEVEL=error

# Copilot CLI sign-in directory the bridge reads. ./bin/ghcp-models reads it
# too. ~ and ~/ are expanded.
# Default: ~/.copilot.
# Change when: you run the Copilot CLI with a different COPILOT_HOME.
# COPILOT_HOME=~/.copilot

# Copilot CLI or runtime the Copilot SDK starts.
# Default: none; the SDK uses the runtime bundled with its npm package.
# Change when: you need to test a different Copilot runtime build.
# COPILOT_CLI_PATH=/absolute/path/to/copilot


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Only for a bridge you start by hand (npm run bridge, which runs
#    node src/server.mjs)
#
# claude-ghcp sets HOST, PORT and BRIDGE_API_KEY itself for both its private
# -p bridge and the persistent bridge, so exporting them has no effect on it.
# To fix the launcher's port, use GHCP_BRIDGE_PORT.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Address the bridge listens on. A value other than 127.0.0.1, ::1 or
# localhost also needs ALLOW_NON_LOOPBACK=1.
# Default: 127.0.0.1.
# HOST=127.0.0.1

# Port the bridge listens on, from 1 to 65535.
# Default: 4142.
# PORT=4142

# Token every route except GET /health and HEAD /api/hello requires, sent as
# Authorization: Bearer <token> or x-api-key: <token>.
# Default: none. The bridge refuses to start without it, unless
# BRIDGE_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=1.
# BRIDGE_API_KEY=replace-with-a-random-local-token

# 1 allows a HOST that is not loopback. Only the value 1 turns it on.
# Default: off. A bridge reachable from other hosts needs TLS and real
# authentication in front of it; see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md#security-boundaries.
# ALLOW_NON_LOOPBACK=1

# 1 lets the bridge run without BRIDGE_API_KEY and accept every request.
# Only the value 1 turns it on.
# Default: off. Use it only for local experiments.
# BRIDGE_ALLOW_UNAUTHENTICATED=1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. LiteLLM client (bin/claude-litellm)
#
# How Claude Code reaches an existing LiteLLM gateway. See docs/LITELLM.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# LiteLLM proxy root. Required. It must use http or https, have no query or
# fragment, and not end in /v1 (Claude Code appends /v1/messages). Trailing
# slashes are removed. --litellm-base-url overrides it.
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=https://litellm.example.com

# LiteLLM virtual key. Required. Use a scoped virtual key, not the master key.
# LITELLM_API_KEY=replace-with-a-scoped-virtual-key

# Model alias Claude Code starts on. It must be a model_name in the gateway's
# LiteLLM config. --litellm-model overrides it.
# Default: claude-sonnet-5.
# LITELLM_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Aliases behind Claude Code's opus, sonnet and haiku model families. The
# haiku alias also serves Claude Code's small background calls.
# Default for each: the LITELLM_MODEL value.
# Change when: a family should route to a different alias, for example
# background calls to a cheaper model.
# LITELLM_OPUS_MODEL=claude-opus-5.5
# LITELLM_SONNET_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# LITELLM_HAIKU_MODEL=claude-haiku-4.5


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. LiteLLM gateway (scripts/start-litellm.sh, run by npm run litellm:start)
#
# How the gateway reaches the bridge. Setup: docs/LITELLM.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Bridge root URL, with no /v1 (LiteLLM appends /v1/messages). Required.
# GHCP_BRIDGE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4142

# Bridge token. Required. `node src/bridge-daemon.mjs ensure <model> <port>`
# prints it, and bridge.json in GHCP_DAEMON_DIR holds it. It changes every time
# the bridge is replaced or restarted, so export the new one and restart
# LiteLLM after that. Never commit a real token.
# GHCP_BRIDGE_TOKEN=replace-with-the-token-from-bridge-daemon-ensure

# LiteLLM config file.
# Default: examples/litellm-github-copilot.yaml in this repository.
# LITELLM_CONFIG=/absolute/path/to/litellm-config.yaml

# Address and port LiteLLM listens on.
# Default: 127.0.0.1 and 4000.
# Change LITELLM_HOST only to expose the gateway beyond this machine.
# LITELLM_HOST=127.0.0.1
# LITELLM_PORT=4000

# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY is not read from your environment: the start script always
# sets it from .runtime/litellm-master-key, which npm run litellm:setup creates.
